WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:15.110
I was doomed from the start. Why does one run towards ruin? Why does it hold such a fascination?

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:24.619
Your appreciation has been most intelligent

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.910
i congratulate you on the success of your performance

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:35.050
What I'm saying is that I have lived in the grip of vice and pleasure.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.320
Oscar Wilde

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:43.580
The sentence of the court is that you'll be imprisoned and kept to hard labor for two years

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.929
It was wrong and I have paid.

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:48.880
It will make a Catholic of you yet.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:49.729
Only unlike dear Jesus you have luggage

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.539
I fully intend to effect a reconciliation with my wife

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:59.669
I feel sure that if I was to see him once I would forgive him everything

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.460
Rest assured, I shall never see Lord Alfred Douglas again.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.070
I forbid him to live with that infernal man

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.352
Oscar, let's run away. Somewhere no one could find us.

00:01:09.352 --> 00:01:10.660
You don't know what you're saying

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.068
Then you will never see Constance again

00:01:14.068 --> 00:01:16.665
Not wearing your silk stockings today, Oscar?

00:01:16.665 --> 00:01:17.530
You go too far, sir

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.629
No,  you go too far

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:37.280
You've taken everything: my family, my work, my freedom! Everything!  There's nothing left to take!

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:44.030
Suffering is nothing when there is love. 
 Love is everything

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.549
I must love and be loved, but the price I pay for it

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.570
Mr. Wilde?  How kind of you to speak to me.  You couldn't lend me five pounds, could you?

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:05.890
I'm in mortal combat with this wallpaper, Robbie, and one of us has to go

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.350
You

